src('SRC032','90th Strategic Missile Wing report to FTD (6 Aug 1965) on UFO reports at F.E. Warren, as reproduced on ufohastings.com','90th SMW (SAC); reproduction by R. Hastings','ufohastings.com (author\'s website)','1965-08-06','Official report excerpt (reproduced)','SECONDARY (reproduction of a primary)','https://ufohastings.com/articles/yet-another-nuclear-missile-launch-officer-talks-about-ufos-at-f-e-warren-afb','Blue Book file (Cheyenne WY, Jul-Aug 1965)','excerpt paras 1-2','%s'%A,'INC033;EVD052','Counts: 31 Jul 75 objects/70 personnel; 1 Aug 29/27; 2 Aug 44/46; total 148 objects/143 personnel. Objects mostly round; sizes pinhead-to-nickel naked eye; formations V, echelon, cross, box, tail; colored lights flashing on/off at 1-2 s intervals, alternately bright and dim; no sound; one daytime civilian report (1 Aug) of an oblong object tumbling and splitting.','Excerpt selected by Hastings; not the Anspaugh log; original not examined.','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED','EXAMINED')
src('SRC033','Project 10073 record and 90th SMW addendum (20 Sep 1965) to the 6 Aug report, Cheyenne WY','Col Willard R. Gilbert (90th SMW) / Blue Book (FTD)','USAF Project Blue Book (scan on ufoscans.com)','1965-09-20','Official correspondence with sighting questionnaires (PDF, 14 pp, poor OCR)','PRIMARY (reproduction)','https://www.ufoscans.com/raw/1965/1965-08-9371404-Cheyenne-Wyoming.pdf','Project 10073 record, Cheyenne WY Aug 1965','pp. 1-3','%s'%A,'INC033;EVD053','Addendum describes: civilian guard at Sioux Army Depot reporting to Golf LCF, AF personnel viewing with binoculars at 2145 and 2220 local (two objects ~1 mile apart, North Star size, pale yellow to white, ~30 deg above horizon); a group of nine military personnel with binoculars (star-size object moving west, disappearing and reappearing; another pea-size luminous globe; "on four occasions a roaring jet-like noise at some distance behind"); a three-man Geodetic Survey Team with a 40-power theodolite (object twice a pinhead in the Big Dipper, resolving into three white objects). The Blue Book cover record is "insufficient data".','OCR is garbled; dates of individual sightings not clear; I did not read all 14 pages.','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED','EXAMINED')
src('SRC034','SUNlite 14-3: Project Blue Book review, July-August 1965 (Midwest flap and F.E. Warren sightings)','Tim Printy','SUNlite (astronomyufo.com)','2025','Skeptical review of the Blue Book file','SECONDARY','https://www.astronomyufo.com/UFO/SUNlite14_3.pdf','','pp. 18-26','%s'%A,'INC033;EVD054','Warren/Cheyenne cases 31 Jul-2 Aug: many stars/planets and meteors; each report only a few sentences; no positional data; many sightings ~0500Z; Jupiter, Capella, Saturn, Vega, Altair, Betelgeuse involved; satellites (Echo 2) and aircraft; temperature inversion on all three nights; Blue Book labelled the "Midwest flap" "inversion effect"; no photographs or triangulation; once a few airmen reported, "others around the base joined in"; local UFO officer did not follow up. Individual Blue Book entries for Warren: insufficient data (Echo 2 per Printy), stars/planets (Capella, Arcturus, probably Vega).','Printy is a skeptic and his identifications are inferred from sparse descriptions; he also notes Blue Book dates in this file are unreliable.','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED','EXAMINED')
src('SRC035','The Bolender Draft (Not Memo), Oct 20, 1969 (transcription and commentary)','Fran Ridge / Brad Sparks / Barry Greenwood (NICAP)','NICAP','2006 (upd. 2016)','Transcription of 3-page USAF document','SECONDARY (transcription of primary)','https://nicap.org/Bolender_Memo.htm','Bolender document (released to R. Todd, Jan 1979)','p. 2','%s'%A,'CLM096;EVD057','Quotes verbatim: "reports of unidentified flying objects which could affect national security are made in accordance with JANAP 146 or Air Force Manual 55-11, and are not part of the Blue Book system (Atch 10)"; also "there is still, however, no evidence that Project Blue Book reports have served any intelligence function (Atch 8)"; recommends terminating Blue Book. NICAP calls it a draft, not a memo; 16 attachments not found by USAF.','Advocacy-site transcription; status of the document (draft vs sent) not resolved; I did not see the scan.','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED','EXAMINED')
